WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
The Rose of Versailles

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
The Rose of Versailles

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.280
Why has the Seine become so murky?

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.450
Where has Paris, the city of flowers gone?

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.910
Everyone goes mad over a piece of bread.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:27.510
Where did the Seine, where people sung about flowers
and spoke of love on its banks, flow away to?

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.690
<i>Winter of 1788.</i>

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.700
<i>The political chaos and the royal
household's financial crisis,</i>

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.230
<i>led to new taxes being imposed one after another.</i>

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.700
<i>The French people's dissatisfaction and
poverty had already reached its limits.</i>

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.150
<i>Despite that, Versailles tried
to retain its authority.</i>

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.280
If you wish to forcibly pass this through...

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.830
...and introduce a new tax to
borrow 420 million livres,

00:00:57.830 --> 00:00:59.760
I urge you to convene the Estates-General.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.720
Not only the First and Second Estates,
which consist of the clergy and nobility.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.330
but it should include representatives from the
Third Estate, the commoner's class, as well.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.030
It should be an Estates-General
where every Estate is represented.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.130
Your Majesty!

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:12.700
There is no other way to overcome the royal
household's current financial crisis,

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.240
which is inflated by debts!

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:21.010
By doing so, there's a possibility that every noble,
clergy and commoner will agree to this new tax.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.980
Please make a decision as our King!

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.280
Wait a second!

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.150
Are you suggesting we let the commoners
have a say in policies?!

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.120
Absolutely not!

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:30.940
You mustn't allow that, Your Majesty!

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:34.360
The commoners are growing increasingly
arrogant as it is already!

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.900
We mustn't let them undermine
your authority any further!

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:42.370
After 200 years, now is the time
to reconvene the Estates-General!

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:55.520
<i>Thus, the prelude to the French Revolution began
with the dissent of a handful of nobles,</i>

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:02.050
<i>which sought to rule France in place of the King,
by gathering the populace's support.</i>

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:05.330
The Estates-General! The Estates-General!

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.060
The Estates-General! The Estates-General!

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.570
Send our representatives to the general assembly!

