00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:51.590
episode

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:51.590
"The Funeral Bells

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:51.590
Toll Amidst the Twilight"

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.300
The antiquated status quo is about
to come crumbling down!

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:04.600
The discrimination between the First, Second
and Third Estates will be abolished!

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.120
Bernard...

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.690
A day will come when we can all live as equals!

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.290
All men are created equal!

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.000
Bernard!

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.990
Hey, Bernard!

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:27.980
André?!

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.040
André, it's you!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.620
I heard your speech just now.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.510
It was brilliant.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.290
Thank you.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.220
Oh, that's right!

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.960
There's someone I want to introduce you to.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.020
Come to my house.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:38.960
It's close by.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.200
My! André!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:45.890
Welcome!

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:46.990
Rosalie?!

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.010
It's really been a while, hasn't it?

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.670
A while is an understatement!

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.140
What have you been doing all this time?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.640
You haven't written to us at all.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.990
More... More importantly...

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:59.180
What are you doing here with Bernard?

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.440
I don't understand what's happening.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.740
Are you two married?!

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:07.700
Yeah, we married shortly after
that Black Knight incident.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.820
I see... So that's why!

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:10.460
Congratulations!

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:11.810
Um...

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.160
Is Lady Oscar well?

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:16.090
Yeah, she's great.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.830
Since then, she transferred from the
Royal Guards to the French Guards,

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:20.800
but she's working hard as always!

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:25.440
Don't worry, Rosalie.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.930
No one has changed since then.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:29.510
Everyone is the same.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.400
The Estates-General!

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.240
Send our representatives to the general assembly!

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:38.320
He's right.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.990
The people, society... Not a single thing
has changed. But change is coming!

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:47.890
André, I have to go to work now,
but please make yourself at home.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.590
I'll take you up on your offer then.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:50.450
Thank you, Rosalie.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.590
Please be sure to give Lady Oscar my regards.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:57.800
Yeah.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.530
Next time, let's all get together.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:06.640
Rosalie is working at Monsieur
Robespierre's organization with me.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:10.240
She went to make handbills and
posters for our next rally just now.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:13.350
You both seem so happy.
You really do...

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:15.020
André,

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.680
won't you join us?

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:20.920
I hardly think you're the type to be content
with merely being a noble's stablehand!

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.260
This coffee is very good.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.410
It has a humble flavor and was poured with love.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:28.830
Then, why were you listening to my speech?

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.120
Why were you attending that rally?

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:34.110
I just happened to have the day off.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.770
I had some time.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:36.410
That's all.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:43.520
Bernard!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:44.710
Bernard!

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.290
They just announced it!

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:49.560
The decree convoking the Estates-General
was just announced!

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:50.460
What?!

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.090
Is that true?!

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.800
<i>On January 1789,</i>

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.540
<i>King Louis XVI, by royal decree, called for
the Estates-General to be convened,</i>

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:08.970
<i>on the first of May at Versailles.</i>

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:16.040
<i>Convoking the Estates-General also meant
it would limit the King's absolute authority,</i>

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:21.310
<i>but even Louis XVI could no longer put a
stop to the changing course of history.</i>

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.250
<i>The Castle of Meudon.</i>

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:31.760
<i>It was an old castle where the Queen had moved
to for her sickly son Joseph, the Dauphin.</i>

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.700
I am Brigadier Oscar François de Jarjayes!

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:37.650
I have come here at Lady Antoinette's urgent request!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.700
Convey to her that I have arrived!

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:46.900
Lady Antoinette!

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.380
Oscar!

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:52.020
Thank goodness you came, Oscar!

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.620
Joseph has been desperately wanting to see you.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.020
His Highness has?

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.960
It's uncertain if he'll live another 6 months.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:01.760
His spine is terribly jagged and
even his ribs are crooked now.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.290
The terminal stages of spinal
caries are already showing.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.730
He only just turned 7...

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.300
Be quiet!

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.140
Go away!

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.570
Your Highness, you mustn't!

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:16.680
Your Highness!

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.180
I'm going outside!

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.640
I want to go out!

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.350
Let me go!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:21.080
Go away!

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.080
Joseph!

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.140
Your Highness.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.350
Oscar...!

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:27.920
It is a pleasure to see you.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.320
Forgive me for not visiting sooner.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:30.650
Oscar...

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:32.530
Oscar...!

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:34.780
Yes, Your Highness.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.330
Please... Please take me outside!

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.700
Please let me ride your horse!

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:41.420
Your Highness...

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.240
I want to ride on a horse with you, Oscar!

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.380
It's all right, Oscar.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:50.090
Please... Please grant my son's wish...

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:51.760
Yes!

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.030
Gallop! Gallop! Gallop!

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:56.800
Gallop! Gallop! Gallop!

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.510
Gallop! Gallop! Gallop!

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:00.240
You mustn't press the horse so hard.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:02.660
Gallop! Gallop! Gallop! Gallop!

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:03.420
Gallop! Gallop! Gallop! Gallop!

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.170
Gallop! Gallop! Gallop! Gallop!

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:04.650
Gallop! Gallop! Gallop! Gallop!

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:16.590
I wish we could keep on riding
like this, forever and ever...

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.760
Your Highness?

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.390
Are you all right, Your Highness?

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:37.800
Perhaps we should start heading back.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:41.260
I hear the Estates-General is
finally going to be convened.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.090
Yes.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.600
I'll be sure to return to the
Palace of Versailles for it.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:50.200
As I'm sure the day will be forever
etched into France's history...

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:53.280
Our France, which I'll rule someday...

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:56.770
Yes, indeed.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.620
Your Highness will someday become Louis XVII.

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:07.240
I love you.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:13.080
Next time, I'm born into this world, I'll be healthy
and won't get sick. I'll grow up strong...

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:15.620
...and become a fine young man...

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:18.150
So wait for me until then!

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:30.770
God, please let Louis Joseph live another month.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:32.270
No, even a week!

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.710
Please let him live to see another day.

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:37.230
Please, I beg you...

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:46.080
Please excuse me.

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.230
Oh, Your Majesty...

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:54.990
Let us pray together.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:55.960
Yes.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.310
Hey, it's Alain!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:21.410
Squad Leader!

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.060
Long time no see, everyone.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.370
Count me in again.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:27.200
Must have been hard about Diane.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.030
Such a sad thing to happen to her.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:30.900
We heard your mother passed
away soon after, too...

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.200
What have you been doing for six months?

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:34.230
We assumed you weren't coming back.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.760
Yeah, I wasn't planning on coming back either.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.910
I buried Mom and Diane in the countryside
where you can see the ocean.

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:44.470
I had planned to live there,
watching over their graves...

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.970
But once the rain lets up, it'll be May.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:50.400
If the Estates-General is being convened,
I felt I had to come back.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:52.720
I want to get a close look on how the...

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.820
...representatives of the Third Estate
will grill the nobility.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.160
Hey, André.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.280
I'll be sure to watch what your blind eye can't see.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:06.530
Oscar.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:09.240
Count Fersen returned to Sweden apparently.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.760
The army delivered a message
conveying his regards to you.

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:14.040
Oscar...?

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.750
André, tell the others we'll begin
the special security training...

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.610
...for the Estates-General tomorrow.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.550
All right.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:39.570
<i>On May 4th, 1789, the day before the
opening ceremony of the Estates-General,</i>

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:43.370
<i>a grand mass was held at the
Church of Saint-Louis in Versailles,</i>

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:46.170
<i>with every representative in attendance.</i>

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:50.910
<i>The procession of representatives
heading to the church,</i>

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:54.180
<i>were guarded by the 1st French Regiment,
known as the French Guards,</i>

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.780
<i>and the Swiss Royal Guards Regiment.</i>

00:12:58.150 --> 00:12:59.840
<i>His Highness must surely be watching.</i>

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:02.690
<i>From one of those windows in
the Palace of Versailles...</i>

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:05.280
<i>He returned from Meudon for this day, after all.</i>

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.300
I wonder if that's where Oscar is?

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.400
The French Guards' helmets are shining.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.650
<i>I love you.</i>

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.150
<i>I'll grow up to be a fine young man.</i>

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.910
<i>So wait for me until then!</i>

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.040
Everyone is in position!

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:31.830
Awaiting orders now!

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.990
André, I almost became a Queen.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.200
The procession will begin shortly.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:42.960
Please be ready.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:45.130
Joseph, I'll be going now.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.600
Brother, I'm going, too.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:49.300
I'll be riding in the same carriage
as Mother in the procession.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.270
Louis-Charles, go now.

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:54.640
And watch closely... in my stead.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:58.270
After all, it's possible you
may become the next Dauphin.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.980
Present, arms!

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:12.260
<i>Marching through the thick crowd
which had lined the streets,</i>

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:15.880
<i>the representatives of the Estates-General
headed towards the Church of Saint-Louis.</i>

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:21.400
<i>At the head of the procession, dressed in all black,
were the 621 representatives of the Third Estate.</i>

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.910
<i>The gaudiness of the nobles,
which followed behind them,</i>

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:27.800
<i>seemed almost shameless in the eyes of the people.</i>

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:37.840
<i>Maximilien de Robespierre, representing
the province of Artois, was 31 years old.</i>

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:41.020
<i>He would eventually become
the future ruler of France.</i>

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:43.650
<i>The commoners' representatives numbered 621.</i>

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.230
<i>However, among their ranks were also nobles,</i>

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:50.860
<i>who were elected as representative of the Third
Estate, with the support of the commoners.</i>

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:54.870
<i>The privilege of being a noble, no longer
held any meaning in the current times.</i>

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:59.070
<i>Let alone the military, which existed for
the sake of the royal household...</i>

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:04.450
Your Highness, Louis Joseph!

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:05.380
Your Highness!

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:06.650
Oh no! Call the doctor!

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:07.350
Your Highness!

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:09.250
Take him to Meudon immediately!

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.250
Prepare the carriage!

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:10.550
Your Highness!

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:16.420
<i>The next day, on May 5th 1789,</i>

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:21.400
<i>the opening ceremony of the Estates-General took
place in the great hall of Hôtel des Menus Plaisirs.</i>

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:22.930
Where is the messenger from Meudon?

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:23.930
How is the Dauphin?

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.670
How is Joseph feeling?

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:28.440
Your Majesty, the opening
ceremony is about to begin.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:32.870
As the Queen of France, attending the opening
ceremony of the Estates-General is your duty.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:35.580
Presenting His Royal Majesty!

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:49.130
Presenting Her Royal Majesty!

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:57.160
<i>There was no applause.</i>

00:15:57.160 --> 00:16:01.770
<i>Not only from the representatives of the
Third Estate, but from the nobility, as well.</i>

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:04.400
<i>Not one person applauded Antoinette.</i>

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:10.410
<i>At this moment, amid the frozen silence,
the Queen realized for certain,</i>

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.610
<i>that the attacks and hatred of the French people...</i>

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:18.320
<i>...weren't directed at the King
or the royal household,</i>

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:22.830
<i>but only to Queen Marie Antoinette herself.</i>

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:26.890
<i>A battle is about to begin.</i>

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:31.270
<i>Now that it's come to this, I won't run or hide!</i>

00:16:31.270 --> 00:16:33.170
<i>After all... I am the Queen of France!</i>

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:46.690
It's been a month since the Estates-General
began and not one day off.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.980
It seems they're at an impasse.

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:51.930
I heard the commoners' representatives...

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:55.660
...are unleashing a fiery debate
on the clergy and nobility.

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:58.870
If only I could join them!

00:16:58.870 --> 00:16:59.580
Oh, here she comes.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.000
Commander, what's it like in there?

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.130
Disorderly as usual.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:11.350
Once the assembly is adjourned,
you'll all get some time off.

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:13.920
I realize you haven't had
a day off, but try to endure.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:17.100
What's this doing here? How unsafe.

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.890
The representatives might injure
themselves when they leave.

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:22.850
I told you to clear the area
of such objects beforehand.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.220
I'm sorry.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:25.390
I didn't notice it.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.900
Throw it away.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:28.810
Yes!

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:40.020
Sheesh, what a terrible catch, André!

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:41.370
It's all right. I'll clean it up.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.040
André, is your right eye...?

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.000
What is it?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:50.920
Who wouldn't feel dazed,
standing like this day after day?

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:51.960
Isn't that right, André?

00:17:52.890 --> 00:17:54.170
Right, yeah...

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:56.320
Maybe I'm a bit tired.

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.680
I might be dazed from the sun.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.640
I see... If that's really all it is then...

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:09.190
Lady Antoinette's carriage...

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:28.490
Rain again...

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.840
The Dauphin's condition must be really dire...

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:35.300
...for the Estates-General to be adjourned and
the King and Queen rushing over to Meudon.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.660
He'll be all right.

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:38.760
Similar incidents have happened
many times before.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:41.720
I'm certain he'll pull through this time, too.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:43.350
I hope that's the case...

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:47.020
That aside, I have another
worrisome thing on hand.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.520
Oh? What could that be?

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:57.240
André.

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.610
What's the matter? Are you checking my eye?

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:04.880
Can you really see this?

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:06.080
What are you talking about?

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:06.900
Of course I can.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:07.960
It's a knife.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:12.930
Made in 1612, it's been handed down for generations
in the Jarjayes family and is your favorite.

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:15.240
So your eye is really all right?

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.470
Stop asking already. It's not funny.

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:20.700
I'm sorry.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:26.550
What's the matter, Oscar?

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:27.950
Do you hear something?

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.490
It's the bells of Notre Dame...!

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:49.900
The Dauphin is in critical condition!

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:52.160
<i>On June 2nd, at 10 o'clock,</i>

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:55.740
<i>the bells of Notre Dame Cathedral tolled solemnly.</i>

00:19:55.740 --> 00:20:00.920
<i>It signaled the beginning of the 40 hour long vigil
for the Dauphin, who was in critical condition.</i>

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:06.930
Joseph...

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:06.930
Joseph.

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:09.890
Father, Mother...

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:11.310
Joseph...!

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:13.400
I know you both must be busy...

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:14.280
I'm sorry...

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:16.730
Joseph...

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.770
Is the Estates-General at an impasse?

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:25.740
Why... Why can't the representatives get
along and come to a compromise?

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:26.740
Joseph...

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:30.500
You don't have to worry
about such things, Joseph...

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:31.680
My dear Joseph...

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:35.740
Just once more... Just once more,
I wish I could go back to Versailles...

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:37.540
Of course you will.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:40.760
She's right. Of course you will, Joseph.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:45.100
Get better and the three of us will return to
Versailles together in the same carriage.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.230
I know!

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:50.530
I'll get your favorite, Oscar François
to be in charge of guarding our carriage.

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:51.270
Yes, let's do that!

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.140
The lady on a white horse...

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:56.130
Her blonde hair in the wind...

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.020
Joseph! Joseph!

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:11.820
Joseph! Joseph!

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:13.520
Don't leave your mother behind!

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:14.960
Ah, God...!

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:39.570
He was just 7 years and 8 months old...

00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:45.820
<i>On June 4th, at one in the morning,</i>

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:50.040
<i>came the tragic and untimely death
of the Dauphin, Louis Joseph.</i>

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:56.690
<i>But perhaps, that he died unaware of the hardships the royal family would face...</i>

00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:58.800
<i>...was a blessing in disguise.</i>

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:03.060
I'm going to Meudon Castle
to offer my condolences.

00:22:09.940 --> 00:22:15.140
<i>Shaken to its core, what course will France take
with the convening of the Estates-General?</i>

00:22:15.820 --> 00:22:21.520
<i>Furthermore, those left behind and
those trying to survive the new era,</i>

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:23.360
<i>what course must they take?</i>

00:22:28.870 --> 00:22:33.330
To be continued

